WEBVTT

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.850
So this is the black camellia.

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:49.530
Her fortune just went flying.

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:50.570
Yup.

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:55.620
<i>A clock that destroys the owner's fortune...</i>

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.700
Miss Nagi! Maria-san!

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:04.250
<i>...and brings them bad luck.</i>

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:09.480
<i>Anyone who obtains it gets cursed.</i>

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:04.930
What're you doing, Hinagiku-san?

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:06.990
That's my line!

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:08.550
Just put something on!

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:11.530
What's going on, Hayate?

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:12.980
What's all the commotion?

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:20.030
What do you think you're doing?!

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:23.000
You misunderstand, Miss Nagi!

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:29.960
Is this bringing me bad luck?

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:31.530
I wonder.

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:34.570
But isn't seeing Hinagiku-san in

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:36.610
only a towel <i>good</i> luck?

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:40.060
Well, if you look at it that way, sure.

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:42.510
What do you mean, "sure"?

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:45.120
You're glad you saw Hinagiku naked?

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:47.790
I didn't say that!

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:49.930
I've seen Hinagiku-san's immodest outfits

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:52.370
quite frequently in the apartment, anyway.

00:03:52.990 --> 00:03:55.860
I haven't given you <i>that</i> much to see!

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:58.740
You put up with so much.

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:00.060
Y-Yes.

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:02.130
That's my line!

00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:06.140
Hayata-kun and the gang 
are in Las Vegas, too?

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:08.530
Yeah, they're at that hotel.

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:11.220
Hina-san's tired from the 
flight, so she's resting.

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:12.350
Oh.

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:13.620
I wanna see them!

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:15.730
Let's go check on them.

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:18.690
Why are you three in Las Vegas?

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:23.200
Well, our flight happened
 to come this way...

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:26.950
Why are you guys in Las Vegas?

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:29.980
We're dealing with a slight problem.

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:31.030
A problem?

00:04:31.030 --> 00:04:33.860
My little sister Tsugumi was kidnapped.

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:34.830
Kidnapped?

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:38.000
Well, "kidnapped" may be a...

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:40.460
What? Nagi-chan's little sister was...

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:41.510
Kidnapped?

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:44.830
Hey! What kind of entry was that?

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:47.140
And why are you guys here?

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:50.600
Stress about the details and 
you'll go bald, Hayata-kun!

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:52.350
Back to the kidnapping.

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:53.950
That's huge!

00:04:53.950 --> 00:04:56.540
Let's call Jack Bauer of 
the Counter Terrorist Unit!

00:04:56.540 --> 00:05:01.290
No, no. It's less of a 
kidnapping and more of a prank.

00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:02.870
A ransom note!

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:03.670
Where, where?

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:05.360
Let me see! Let me see!

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:07.870
<b><i>We have Ruri Tsugumi. 
Come to Las Vegas if you want her to live. 
We'll exchange her for the black camellia.
We'll do a trade under the big tree 
at 9 p.m. on 9/24. 
Bring the black camellia!</i></b>

00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:07.090
See?

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:09.920
It's not that big of a deal.

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:13.270
It's real!

00:05:13.270 --> 00:05:15.250
It's a real kidnapping!

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:16.580
What?

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:18.500
We can't just stand here!

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:20.220
Let us handle this!

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:22.410
We'll arrest the kidnappers!

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:23.590
Arrest them!

00:05:24.730 --> 00:05:28.050
No, no. Don't do 
anything unnecessary!

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:31.390
This is bad, Hayate! Stop those idiots!

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:32.890
Yes, ma'am!

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:35.230
Wait, you guys!

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:48.450
I'm sorry! Are you all right?

00:05:52.130 --> 00:05:54.700
Chiharu-san? Kayura-san?

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:56.910
Ayasaki-kun?

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:58.700
Why are you here?

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:00.330
What about you two?

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:02.880
Forget that. Where'd my glasses go?

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:05.880
Um... Uh...

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:09.020
I am so sorry! So sorry!

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:10.280
I'll go and...

00:06:10.280 --> 00:06:11.950
Don't worry about it.

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:23.440
No "oohs" and "aahs"!

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:25.640
Now isn't the time!

00:06:25.640 --> 00:06:29.450
Hurry, or else those stupid 
girls will go to the police!

00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:32.160
S-Sorry!

00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:34.440
Geez.

00:06:37.310 --> 00:06:40.680
But seriously, what're you doing in America?

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:43.350
Weren't you gonna relax at home?

00:06:43.350 --> 00:06:45.200
I have my reasons.

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:46.000
Reasons?

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:48.700
And what are you guys doing here?

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:50.380
This isn't your hotel.

00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:53.020
Right.

00:06:53.020 --> 00:06:56.890
We ran into some trouble, 
so we wound up here by chance.

00:06:57.310 --> 00:06:58.740
By chance?

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:05.100
We've got a problem! CTU!

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:08.280
Connect me to Jack Bauer 
in the CTU right away!

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:10.230
What?

00:07:10.230 --> 00:07:12.280
There's no CTU and 
nobody by that name?

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:15.870
Then we need Rikiya! Call him!

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:18.030
Cut it out!

00:07:19.510 --> 00:07:21.410
Listen, everyone.

00:07:21.410 --> 00:07:23.710
This kidnapping is no joke.

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:29.710
What has the black suit said?

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:32.710
I understand Japanese a little...

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:36.710
He said, "I'm going to 
kidnap someone seriously."

00:07:37.410 --> 00:07:40.290
Give me back the ransom note.

00:07:40.290 --> 00:07:41.550
No, no!

00:07:41.550 --> 00:07:44.230
It's hard to get your 
hands on a ransom note.

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:46.470
<i>I can't do it, Hayata-kun. 
Not even for you.</i>

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:47.220
"And there is a ransom note, which I wrote!"

00:07:46.470 --> 00:07:48.650
<i>What if you lose it?</i>

00:07:47.460 --> 00:07:47.930
Huh?!

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:51.150
What a pain in the ass.

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:54.410
I'll take it by force. Forgive me!

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:57.260
No, stop! Stop!

00:07:55.480 --> 00:07:57.260
<i>By force...</i>

00:07:57.260 --> 00:07:59.290
Stop goofing around!

00:08:00.260 --> 00:08:03.170
That tickles! Stop touching 
me there, Hayata-kun!

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:04.450
Freeze!

00:08:04.730 --> 00:08:05.670
Huh?

00:08:07.650 --> 00:08:08.370
Hold up!

00:08:08.890 --> 00:08:11.750
I-It's not what you think! We were just...

00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:12.580
Don't move!

00:08:14.190 --> 00:08:16.580
No, um...

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:25.250
<i>A clock that destroys the owner's 
fortune and brings them bad luck.</i>

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:34.590
What are you thinking?

00:08:34.600 --> 00:08:36.190
I'm scared!

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:40.420
Why all the ruckus?

00:08:40.420 --> 00:08:42.060
What're you doing?

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:43.910
I'm sorry.

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:46.460
I was trying to get the 
ransom note back when...

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:49.770
What? If you cause problems here,

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:52.400
we won't be able to
 deal with Tsugumi later.

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:54.840
Hayate, get out of here!

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:56.470
Y-Yes.

00:08:58.490 --> 00:09:00.740
This is going to be hard to fix.

00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:03.160
What does he think he's doing?

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:04.260
Excuse me.

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:08.930
Did you see the black suit guy 
of the public indecency

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:11.600
who had assaulted women around here?

00:09:12.090 --> 00:09:13.240
<i>Indecency?</i>

00:09:14.510 --> 00:09:16.100
I don't know.

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:19.910
Indecency...?

00:09:20.480 --> 00:09:24.020
What is Hayate doing?

00:09:29.530 --> 00:09:31.740
It's already 8:30 p.m.

00:09:33.850 --> 00:09:36.260
This really is a cursed clock.

00:09:37.060 --> 00:09:39.040
Then will I really have

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:41.870
incredible luck when the 
 hands strike eight?

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:46.270
Oh?

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:49.270
What's going on, Ayasaki-kun?

00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:54.020
I'm not surprised you're here.

00:09:54.020 --> 00:09:58.520
And what airplane trouble 
brought you here, Teacher?

00:09:58.520 --> 00:10:00.140
What are you talking about?

00:10:00.140 --> 00:10:03.420
I'm here to gamble for 
millions in Las Vegas.

00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:08.540
See, I even rented a car big enough 
to carry the riches I could win.

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:12.090
That's nice... Though pointless.

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:14.410
What's with the clock?

00:10:15.410 --> 00:10:19.380
This is a cursed clock that 
brings bad luck to its owner.

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:20.050
Huh?

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:22.550
Why do you have it?

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:25.470
For many reasons.

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:29.620
However, when both hands strike eight,

00:10:29.620 --> 00:10:32.060
its owner will have incredible luck.

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:37.320
So if I play the slots right then, I'll win big?

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:39.780
Wouldn't that be nice?

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:41.670
Actually, it's almost time.

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:46.790
Whoa, Teacher! Don't!

00:10:52.950 --> 00:10:58.550
I-I won! I'm a billionaire!

00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:02.560
What a mess.

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:04.430
That Hayata-kun.

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:05.940
Now, now.

00:11:06.650 --> 00:11:07.390
Huh?

00:11:07.570 --> 00:11:10.470
Yay, yay! I'm rich!

00:11:10.470 --> 00:11:12.290
What's up with Yukiji?

00:11:12.290 --> 00:11:15.380
I bet she's up to no good.

00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:16.000
<i>I'm gonna quit my job!</i>

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:19.650
Yes, that's right.

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:24.430
I want you to buy the best car 
out there tomorrow. Please!

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:31.180
Who would've imagined this 
clock would win me millions?

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:35.480
This clock is the best.

00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:36.520
Hey.

00:11:37.900 --> 00:11:39.720
Give me everything you've got.

00:11:43.230 --> 00:11:45.030
Oh! Found you.

00:11:45.810 --> 00:11:47.040
Teacher.

00:11:49.510 --> 00:11:50.930
Teacher?

00:11:52.420 --> 00:11:54.440
Ayasaki-kun.

00:11:55.930 --> 00:11:59.440
Hey, what happened? Where's the clock?

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:03.320
It was stolen with my money.

00:12:03.810 --> 00:12:05.970
What?

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:10.410
The black camellia was stolen?

00:12:10.780 --> 00:12:12.260
I'm so sorry.

00:12:12.260 --> 00:12:14.420
I looked away for a moment, and...

00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:17.210
Why weren't you paying attention?

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:19.470
Well, um...

00:12:19.470 --> 00:12:22.360
Teacher Katsura showed up, 
 and then on the slots...

00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:23.800
The slots?!

00:12:23.990 --> 00:12:25.480
Hayate, you idiot!

00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:29.560
Tsugumi's life may be in danger, 
and you're playing the slots?

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:33.280
I wasn't the one playing.

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:37.290
Whatever! Just go get 
the black camellia back.

00:12:37.290 --> 00:12:38.440
O-Okay.

00:12:38.850 --> 00:12:40.690
It's almost time for the trade.

00:12:40.690 --> 00:12:43.520
You have to find it before then.

00:12:43.520 --> 00:12:46.160
If something happens to Tsugumi, 
it's your fault, Hayate!

00:12:46.430 --> 00:12:47.690
I understand!

00:12:55.100 --> 00:12:57.380
Weren't you a bit harsh?

00:12:58.900 --> 00:13:00.090
Shut up!

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:03.030
It's almost time for the trade.

00:13:03.030 --> 00:13:05.630
I'll cover for his mistake.

00:13:06.530 --> 00:13:08.140
Cover?

00:13:08.710 --> 00:13:14.390
I'll go there myself and take 
care of it somehow... so...

00:13:14.990 --> 00:13:18.230
M-Maria, you go help Hayate.

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:19.790
Please.

00:13:25.020 --> 00:13:27.410
It must be hard on Hayate-kun,

00:13:27.720 --> 00:13:30.700
with a master who's always 
getting so angry at him.

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:33.520
Wh-What?

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:36.920
I'm worried about Nagi going on her own.

00:13:38.470 --> 00:13:42.020
We'll accompany her.

00:13:55.560 --> 00:13:57.340
I can't find it.

00:13:57.340 --> 00:13:59.540
America is huge.

00:14:00.850 --> 00:14:03.520
What should we do, Ayasaki-kun?

00:14:03.520 --> 00:14:07.220
You're asking me? 
Without any clues, I don't...

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:10.180
Hey, Hayata-kun! Yukiji!

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:13.200
Oh, Hanabishi-san. Asakaze-san.

00:14:13.590 --> 00:14:15.750
Do you know where Izumi is?

00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:17.960
You mean Segawa-san?

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:21.370
She said she'd thought of a new prank.

00:14:21.370 --> 00:14:23.460
And we haven't seen her since.

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:25.120
That's worrisome.

00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:27.340
I wonder where she went?

00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:32.220
Hello? Hina-chan?

00:14:32.800 --> 00:14:38.230
I was hiding in the car earlier, 
planning to scare Katsura-chan,

00:14:38.660 --> 00:14:40.800
<i>but something terrible happened.</i>

00:14:44.690 --> 00:14:46.720
Hayate-kun! Big sister!

00:14:53.630 --> 00:14:55.950
It's so far.

00:14:56.390 --> 00:14:58.700
Are we there yet?

00:14:58.700 --> 00:14:59.960
You said it.

00:15:01.770 --> 00:15:04.460
I-I think we're getting close.

00:15:15.190 --> 00:15:17.030
It's really this way?

00:15:17.030 --> 00:15:18.860
I think it's over there.

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:23.300
What's that?

00:15:27.300 --> 00:15:30.780
This is the middle of the desert.

00:15:31.980 --> 00:15:33.150
That's...

00:15:45.430 --> 00:15:47.760
Tsugumi! Where are you?

00:15:48.690 --> 00:15:51.090
If you can hear me, answer!

00:15:51.090 --> 00:15:53.760
Tsugumi! Tsugumi!

00:15:55.620 --> 00:15:57.150
Good evening.

00:16:06.130 --> 00:16:09.190
Did you bring me the black camellia?

00:16:12.650 --> 00:16:14.380
Who's that?

00:16:16.100 --> 00:16:18.700
Well, then...

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:24.270
I'll take the black camellia now.

00:16:25.850 --> 00:16:29.130
Sorry, but the black camellia was stolen.

00:16:31.200 --> 00:16:32.780
It was stolen.

00:16:33.430 --> 00:16:34.390
So I don't have it!

00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:37.510
Sto...len?

00:16:37.980 --> 00:16:41.080
But Hayate's trying to find it, so...

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:42.270
It was stolen?

00:16:42.710 --> 00:16:48.230
I won't let this go so easily!

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:52.570
What's going on?

00:16:54.480 --> 00:16:55.660
Shidou!

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:56.740
Tsugumi!

00:16:56.740 --> 00:16:59.370
Both of you! Go find the black camellia!

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:00.180
Yes!

00:17:00.180 --> 00:17:01.250
Of course.

00:17:06.350 --> 00:17:07.250
Tsugumi!

00:17:08.860 --> 00:17:09.920
Big sister?

00:17:11.180 --> 00:17:13.510
I thought you were kidnapped.

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:15.080
I... Um...

00:17:15.080 --> 00:17:17.010
Miss Nagi!

00:17:19.110 --> 00:17:21.000
Maria-sama just called.

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:22.990
We located the black camellia.

00:17:22.990 --> 00:17:24.290
Really?

00:17:24.290 --> 00:17:25.520
Yes, it's...

00:17:26.160 --> 00:17:28.650
If that's the case...

00:17:30.340 --> 00:17:32.740
Go get it, quick!

00:17:38.990 --> 00:17:39.830
Nagi!

00:17:44.150 --> 00:17:47.960
Until then, we'll take Nagi 
Sanzenin as our hostage.

00:17:48.200 --> 00:17:49.590
Hey, wait!

00:17:50.160 --> 00:17:51.410
 Fire Amulet: Bad Ghosts

00:18:05.140 --> 00:18:06.610
They've disappeared!

00:18:08.710 --> 00:18:14.150
I think we were repelled 
by that demon's realm.

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:16.140
Demon?

00:18:16.140 --> 00:18:17.140
Yes.

00:18:19.440 --> 00:18:23.470
She's not a normal human being.

00:18:26.090 --> 00:18:29.940
Whether she's a demon or not,

00:18:31.440 --> 00:18:35.020
I'll make her regret kidnapping Nagi

00:18:35.900 --> 00:18:38.340
right in front of me.

00:18:38.750 --> 00:18:41.600
<i>Bad. This is bad.</i>

00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:44.100
<i>It's been awhile 
since Isumi-san's lost it.</i>

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:45.880
Hey, black suit!

00:18:45.880 --> 00:18:46.600
Yes!

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:49.940
Call the police right away! Call the FBI!

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:52.090
Catch those thieves immediately!

00:18:52.090 --> 00:18:53.650
Y-Yes!

00:19:21.290 --> 00:19:23.350
Izumi. Big sister!

00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:25.380
Hina-chan!

00:19:25.380 --> 00:19:28.340
Why didn't you wait for the police?

00:19:28.340 --> 00:19:30.940
Because I wanted to get 
it back right away!

00:19:31.290 --> 00:19:33.620
But once you learned 
Izumi was safe,

00:19:33.620 --> 00:19:35.910
you didn't have to act on your own.

00:19:35.910 --> 00:19:37.950
It's my money!

00:19:41.090 --> 00:19:42.110
Hello?

00:19:43.190 --> 00:19:44.110
Ayumu?

00:19:44.770 --> 00:19:46.530
When are the police getting here?

00:19:47.720 --> 00:19:50.820
<i>I think in about 10 minutes.</i>

00:19:50.820 --> 00:19:52.210
Tell them to hurry.

00:19:57.360 --> 00:20:00.380
Hey! We have to go before the cops get here!

00:20:05.740 --> 00:20:06.930
By the way, Segawa-san.

00:20:07.230 --> 00:20:08.440
Yes?

00:20:08.440 --> 00:20:11.180
Did those guys have a clock?

00:20:11.660 --> 00:20:13.560
It looks like a pocket watch.

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:19.360
I think a guy with blond 
hair in a ponytail has it.

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:22.320
A guy with blond hair in a ponytail?

00:20:22.710 --> 00:20:24.950
What? T-Tsugumi-san?

00:20:33.270 --> 00:20:35.820
We didn't have the time to 
get away with the money?

00:20:37.020 --> 00:20:40.420
We went through a lot of 
trouble to steal it after all.

00:20:40.720 --> 00:20:42.000
That's him!

00:20:42.960 --> 00:20:45.140
Wait, Tsugumi-san!

00:20:45.140 --> 00:20:46.590
My money...

00:21:03.540 --> 00:21:06.490
The black camellia is mine!

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:16.030
Mine!

00:21:32.140 --> 00:21:34.700
Be careful, Tsugumi-san!

00:22:00.220 --> 00:22:01.000
Hayate?
